This function is already minimal: one field lookup followed by a validity check. The rewrite keeps the same logic and the same calls, and returns through a single conditional expression. Any speed difference will be marginal.

```cpp
    FIT_BOOL IsAvgCombinedPedalSmoothnessValid() const
    {
        const Field* field = GetField(63);
        return (field != FIT_NULL) ? field->IsValueValid() : FIT_FALSE;
    }
```